ale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D465\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D465\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, is equal to ____________.</p>", "options": [], "correct_options": [], "answer": "762", "explanation": null}, "hi": {"direction": null, "comprehension": null, "content": "\u092e\u093e\u0928 \u0932\u0940\u091c\u093f\u090f \u0915\u093f <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.459ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 645 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D446\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D446\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, \u0909\u0928 \u0938\u092d\u0940 \u0938\u093e\u0924 \u0905\u0902\u0915\u094b\u0902 \u0935\u093e\u0932\u0940 \u0938\u0902\u0916\u094d\u092f\u093e\u0913\u0902 (numbers) \u0915\u093e \u0938\u092e\u0941\u091a\u094d\u091a\u092f (set) \u0939\u0948 \u091c\u094b \u0905\u0902\u0915\u094b\u0902 0,1 \u0914\u0930 2 \u0938\u0947 \u092c\u0928\u093e\u092f\u0940 \u091c\u093e \u0938\u0915\u0924\u0940 \u0939\u0948\u0902\u0964 \u0909\u0926\u093e\u0939\u0930\u0923 \u0915\u0947 \u0932\u093f\u090f, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.459ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 645 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D446\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D446\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> \u092e\u0947\u0902 \u0938\u0902\u0916\u094d\u092f\u093e 2210222 \u0939\u0948, \u092a\u0930\u0928\u094d\u0924\u0941 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.459ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 645 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D446\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D446\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> \u092e\u0947\u0902 \u0938\u0902\u0916\u094d\u092f\u093e 0210222 \u0928\u0939\u0940\u0902 \u0939\u0948\u0964\n\u0924\u092c <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.459ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 645 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D446\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D446\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> \u092e\u0947\u0902 \u0910\u0938\u0947 \u0938\u092d\u0940 \u0905\u0935\u092f\u0935\u094b\u0902 (elements) <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 572 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D465\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D465\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, \u091c\u093f\u0938\u092e\u0947\u0902 \u0905\u0902\u0915\u094b\u0902 0 \u0914\u0930 1 \u092e\u0947\u0902 \u0938\u0947 \u0915\u092e \u0938\u0947 \u0915\u092e \u090f\u0915 \u0905\u0902\u0915 \u0920\u0940\u0915 (exactly) \u0926\u094b \u092c\u093e\u0930 \u0906\u0924\u093e \u0939\u0948, \u0915\u0940 \u0938\u0902\u0916\u094d\u092f\u093e _________ \u0939\u0948\u0964", "options": [], "correct_options": [], "answer": "762", "explanation": null}}, "subject": "mathematics", "timeAllotted": 240000, "topic": "conditional-permutations", "type": "integer", "year": 2025, "yearKey": "jee-advanced-2025-paper-1-online", "active": true, "options": [], "correct_options": ["762"], "explanation": "<p>We form 7-digit numbers using digits $\\{0, 1, 2\\}$. The first digit cannot be $0$, so the first digit must be chosen from $\\{1, 2\\}$.<br>We need the number of elements in $S$ where at least one of $0$ or $1$ appears exactly twice.<br>Let $A$ be the event that digit $0$ appears exactly twice, and $B$ be the event that digit $1$ appears exactly twice.<br>By the principle of inclusion-exclusion:<br>$$|A \\cup B| = |A| + |B| - |A \\cap B|$$<br>\u2022 <b>For |A| (0 appears twice):</b> The first digit can be 1 or 2 (2 choices). The 2 zeros can be placed in any of the remaining 6 places in $\\binom{6}{2} = 15$ ways. The remaining 4 places can be filled with $\\{1, 2\\}$ in $2^4 = 16$ ways: $|A| = 2 \\times 15 \\times 16 = 480$.<br>\u2022 <b>For |B| (1 appears twice):</b><br>Case 1: First digit is 1 (1 choice). Then exactly one more 1 among the remaining 6 places: $\\binom{6}{1} = 6$ ways. The other 5 places are chosen from $\\{0, 2\\}$: $2^5 = 32$ ways $\\implies 1 \\times 6 \\times 32 = 192$.<br>Case 2: First digit is 2 (1 choice). Then two 1s in the remaining 6 places: $\\binom{6}{2} = 15$ ways. The other 4 places from $\\{0, 2\\}$: $2^4 = 16$ ways $\\implies 15 \\times 16 = 240$.<br>Total $|B| = 192 + 240 = 432$.<br>\u2022 <b>For |A &cap; B| (both 0 and 1 appear twice):</b><br>Evaluating the cases yields $|A \\cap B| = 150$.<br>$$|A \\cup B| = 480 + 432 - 150 = 762$$</p>", "qKey": "plet-s-be-the-set-of-all-seven-digit-numbers-that-can-be-jee-advanced-mathematics-z81ein55wkau4ofh", "paperKey": "jee-advanced-2025-paper-1-online", "answer": "762"}], "answer": "762"}